# Aim and Relevance

### Research Topic 

In this collaboration we will try to explore the following topic.

**Optimal point forecast for nonlinear reconciliation**: Recently projection-based and conditioning-based reconciliation methods for time series with nonlinear constraints have been developed. Although some guarantees for improvement over the base forecast has been shown in these studies, an optimal way of obtaining a reconciled point forecast on the nonlinear manifold is yet to be explored. Additionally, multiple options for obtaining a reconciled point forecast on the manifold can be crafted - (i) *projecting the incoherent point forecast*, (ii) *computing the Frechet mean of the reconciled distribution*, or (iii) *computing the Euclidean mean of the reconciled distribution*. We will try to explore which of these methods is more accurate, and if there is an optimal method to obtain the reconciled point forecast which guarantees to achieve the minimum score with respect to an suitable scoring rule metric.


