## Detailed Institutional Responsibilities

To ensure efficient parallel execution of both research tracks over the 3-month cycle, responsibilities are allocated as follows:

- **DACD, SUPSI (Lead & Execution):**
  - Act as primary project coordinators.
  - Lead computational implementation, simulation design, and algorithmic benchmarking for both Topic 1 and Topic 2.
  - Oversee data collection and pipeline preprocessing for applied engineering case studies (e.g., water/energy networks).
- **IDSIA, USI-SUPSI (Scientific Supervision):**
  - Provide methodological guidance on probabilistic forecasting architectures and scoring rules.
  - Oversee the statistical rigor of the benchmarking framework.
  - Co-steer the structure and narrative flow of the methodological manuscript.
- **Department of Statistical Sciences, UniPD (Theoretical Foundations & Hosting):**
  - Drive the mathematical formulations regarding projection geometries and Frechet means on constrained manifolds.
  - Host the 1-month intensive on-site research sprint to finalize theorem proofs and unify the manuscripts.
  - Provide structural domain expertise via their foundational background in hierarchical time series reconciliation.

