## Risk Assessment & Mitigation

Given the compressed 3-month timeline of this collaboration, we identify the following primary risks and corresponding mitigation strategies:

- **Risk 1: Mathematical intractability of optimal point forecasts (Topic 1).**
  - *Mitigation:* If finding a universally optimal closed-form solution with respect to general scoring rules proves impossible within the first 6 weeks, the focus will pivot to a comprehensive empirical comparison of the three candidate heuristics (projected base, Fréchet mean, Euclidean mean) to establish empirical guidelines for publication.

## Software, Data Governance, & Open Science

- **Code Repository:** All computational scripts developed during this collaboration will be maintained in a private GitHub repository shared among the main contacts, to be made fully open-source upon manuscript publication.
- **Data Privacy & GDPR:** This project relies entirely on open-source, aggregated macro-level benchmarks or anonymized industrial simulation data. No personal data or proprietary data subject to GDPR or Swiss Federal Act on Data Protection (FADP) regulations will be processed, removing the need for institutional ethics committee clearance.
